/*****************************************************************************
    tableProbe -- does premise 3's FOUNDATION actually run?

    docs/jitDesign.md premise 3 says: "Type at emit time comes from
    dataNames[datA] -- a CARRIED FACT, not an inference. No type inference pass,
    ever. The field already knows what it is."

    That sentence has never been executed. `dataNames[datA]` appears in exactly
    two places in the tree -- IncantForms/Windows/tabs:36 and
    IncantForms/WorkingOn/tester:57 -- and in BOTH it sits BELOW a `stop()`.
    Tony's own prototype of the table's index lookup is dead code that looks
    live: standing rule H2's exact pathology, and the reason H2 exists.

    So before any table arc work is scheduled on premise 3, this asks the one
    question the premise assumes the answer to: CAN INCANT INDEX A DEFINED LIST
    BY A FIELD'S OWN datA AND GET THE TYPE NAME BACK?

    Rows deliberately span the scalar/non-scalar boundary the fallback column
    is drawn on, because a lookup that works for isCOUNT and silently fails for
    isSTAK would send the arc off with the wrong foundation.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (CLAUDE.md third corollary).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;

register(TableProbe);
define
    dataNames isANY isCHAR isSET isBUFFER isCOUNT isGROUP isITEM isMAP isNUMBER isOBJECT isREGEX isSTAK isSTRING isTOKEN;
    probeCount  = 42;
    probeNumber = 3.5;
    probeString = "words";
    probeEmpty;
    nameOf argument code={
        slot = argument.datA;
        found = dataNames[slot];
        if found != 0;  print + `taG argument "datA=" slot "->" found:;
        else            print + `taG argument "datA=" slot "-> NO ENTRY":;
        };
    runProbe code={
        print "premise 3 foundation -- dataNames[datA]:";
        nameOf(probeCount);
        nameOf(probeNumber);
        nameOf(probeString);
        nameOf(probeEmpty);
        nameOf(dataNames);
        print "is the float a DEFINE-block artifact? assign inside an action:";
        localNum = 3.5;
        nameOf(localNum);
        localNum2 = 7.25;
        print + "localNum2 prints as" localNum2:;
        print "does a node with a LIST carry datA? (T3's open half):";
        listy +% probeCount probeString;
        nameOf(listy);
        };
    ;

runProbe();
print "TP SENTINEL":;
stop();
